through the support of its vertex density"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a9cc53d7-afd6-4e88-96bd-4304b834fef5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13fb7ef4-8225-428b-b6a8-d9ac285d2960"],
 ", Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bedd1fb1-9441-47ac-b6a5-60f0546b610c"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6820aff-a6b2-4aff-a19b-c137be1931e2"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular and hexagonal lattices, before the \
rim, and is the convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f1d96e14-1d90-480e-83a5-17acd01bb046"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shell on the square grid: counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ec162c14-f8b2-4281-ab2f-b952752b6750"],
 ", the coordination sequence; Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77e28907-885e-4f13-8583-b4dc141929dc"],
 ", since a shell is all boundary."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a39b0c7f-e2f0-41d4-bc81-496373fb5209"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Segment on the square grid between vertices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "88633d0a-d4a8-4d82-b77f-0b6c828ef061"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5497c717-9ac6-4557-a3b2-b4c6b3f4827f"],
 " steps apart along the two axes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "708eba52-a628-4011-8110-5caf9412ce71"],
 ": its interval is a rectangle, with counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a871e21e-4ec1-40a1-a8ea-589d63eb8d6f"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aea52fc3-f0ec-4d9e-92dd-029420e8905b"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e4542dc2-ee4b-422d-bc84-871137267f8a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Ball on the discretized plane: the Riemannian measure can exceed the \
counting measure of the smaller ball, when a vertex at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8fba92fb-449d-45b2-a24e-81fd0d1768ce"],
 " has no neighbour at distance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c4a28bad-5a7d-42d0-9819-1fe6bf7a1f80"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e46797ec-c0c4-4ab9-b437-bdd9332e54c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["VolumeGrowthObservables"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/VolumeGrowthObservables", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "7cb0fe56-b08b-418a-a810-fbfcbb299c99"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the dimension and the scalar curvature read from the growth of the balls \
under either measure; it lives on the Riemannian Infrageometry guide"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"f366248f-3cb5-40d5-9f0a-78333279fa9d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Find Functions", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"449db884-6966-48cf-81cb-0ee324ba35f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "c3ddd302-9e67-49f4-a29e-9923cec354af"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a vertex drawn from the candidate pool, narrowed by \"From\" and \"Distance\
\"; a trailing count gives a List of vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"188674c6-9dba-48ee-aa3a-412fc5b9d157"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraMidpoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraMidpoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "a0d02862-ea06-4315-aac0-a78906f00fb0"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the middle vertices of the shortest paths from p1 to p2 as a density, one \
vertex at even distance, two at odd"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"e40481b5-b87d-4c17-a2e8-4e2120195703"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraEquidistantSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraEquidistantSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
